    "standardized_narrative": "At the 2019 year end the syndicate had opening gross claims outstanding of GBP 1,949.6m. Using the syndicate's gross claims development table, prior-year reestimations (2017 and earlier) resulted in a net strengthening of reserves of approximately GBP 28.5m (c.1.46% of opening reserves). The report cites a mix of prior-year releases and deteriorations, with 2019 showing gross and net deteriorations; contributing factors include adverse claims development in some lines, a change in exposure/earnings patterns for certain consumer product and warranty portfolios (a change in accounting estimate / reserve methodology) and development on large losses. Named 2019 catastrophe events (Storm Dorian, Typhoon Faxai and Typhoon Hagibis) are disclosed as 2019 catastrophe costs but the prioryear strengthening above is driven by re-estimation in older underwriting years as shown in the gross claims development triangle.",
